      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "My Turn 4.\n\
I took 2 damage from Sneak (down to 18), they drew a card from Oracle.\n\
Next turn Sneak hits for 1 again, maybe more if they cast another Merfolk, and they draw again. Oracle is a problem for card advantage!\n\
I just drew Angelic Edict (4W). So I can exile Oracle now?\n\
Wait, 4W is 5 mana. I have exactly 5 mana if I play a land (Plains x3, Thriving Heath, Guardian Idol = 5 mana total).\n\
Or I can play Basri's Acolyte this turn, pump Brightmare and Guardian Idol? (Idol isn't a creature unless activated, I can't activate it before casting Acolyte if I want to Acolyte, since I'd need 2 to activate + 2WW to cast = 6 mana).\n\
\n\
I can just exile the Seafloor Oracle right now. That stops the card draw engine. Next turn Sneak hits for 1, whatever.\n\
Wait, let's look at the alternatives.\n\
Basri's Acolyte makes Brightmare a 3/4 and... I have no other creature.\n\
Angelic Edict costs 5 right now precisely. Seafloor Oracle is 2/3.\n\
\n\
Let's do this:\n\
Play a Plains. Tap all 5 sources. Cast Angelic Edict, targeting Oracle.\n\
Then attack with Brightmare for 2.\n\
\n\
Exiling the value engine is smart. `choose_action(choice=\"p16\")` then `choose_action(choice=\"p18\")` (Angelic Edict id) later. Wait, Angelic Edict was just drawn, ID is p28 (from `get_oracle_text`... no, the new card is `Angelic Edict [id=p30]`). Let me check the hand:\n\
Ah, `Angelic Edict` is in hand, I will cast it after playing land.",
