      "reasoning": "I'll chat and then play Basri's Acolyte to build up my board presence.\n\
I should play Plains, then cast Basri's Acolyte, putting +1/+1 counters on Brightmare and Guardian Idol (wait, Idol is not a creature). I can activate Idol for 2 mana, then cast Acolyte for 4 mana? Yes, I have 5 lands + Idol = 6 mana available!\n\
\n\
Let me verify:\n\
Plains + Plains + Plains + Plains + Thriving Heath + Guardian Idol = 6 mana.\n\
Guardian Idol is a mana source but I can use its second ability to make it a 2/2 creature. So: use 2 mana from lands to activate Guardian Idol. Then use remaining 3 lands + Guardian Idol's mana to cast Basri's Acolyte?\n\
Wait, Acolyte costs 2WW.\n\
Let's see: Play Plains. 5 lands. Tap 2 lands, activate Idol. Idol is a 2/2 until EOT.\n\
Now I have 3 lands and Idol. I can tap 3 lands and Idol for 4 mana (2WW) to cast Acolyte.\n\
Acolyte enters, triggers: put a +1/+1 counter on Brightmare and Guardian Idol!\n\
Since Guardian Idol is a noncreature artifact normally, the counter stays on it! Next time I activate it, it will be a 3/3! And it works right now since it's a creature.\n\
Then I attack with Brightmare 3/4 and Idol 3/3!\n\
This is huge!\n\
\n\
Let's execute!\n\
1. Chat: \"Time to go on the offensive! Teamwork makes the dream work!\"\n\
2. Play land (Plains p23).\n\
3. Activate Guardian Idol.\n\
4. Cast Basri's Acolyte.\n\
5. Target Brightmare and Idol.\n\
\n\
First, chat.",
