      "reasoning": "Now cast Acolyte [id=p10].\n\
I have 3 untapped lands + Guardian Idol (which can tap for mana).\n\
Wait, if I tap Guardian Idol for mana, it stops being a blocker/attacker?\n\
No, it's a creature. Creatures can tap for abilities.\n\
Wait, if I tap it for mana, it is tapped. Tapped creatures can't attack.\n\
So I would lose the attack with the Idol.\n\
But I get a permanent +1/+1 counter on it.\n\
Acolyte makes it a 3/3 (permanently, since counters stay on non-creatures too, and it is an artifact). Next turn I can animate it as a 3/3.\n\
And Brightmare becomes 3/4.\n\
Attacking with just Brightmare (3/4) is good pressure.\n\
If I don't tap Idol for mana, I can't cast Acolyte (cost 4, I have 3 lands).\n\
Wait, I have 5 lands total!\n\
I used 2 for Idol activation.\n\
Remaining: 3 lands.\n\
I need 4 mana for Acolyte.\n\
So I MUST tap Idol for mana.\n\
So Idol will be tapped and cannot attack.\n\
That's fine. It gets a counter and becomes a threat for later.\n\
And Brightmare attacks as a 3/4 into their open board (they have 2 mana open? No, 5 Islands, 2 tapped for something? No, all untapped?\n\
Opponent BF: Island (tapped), Island (tapped), Island, Island, Island.\n\
Wait, 3 untapped Islands. They could have bounce or counterspell.\n\
Counterspell would be bad.\n\
But I have to play into it.\n\
Go for it.\n\
\n\
Cast Acolyte. Tap Idol for mana.\n\
Target Brightmare and Idol.",
